{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  P and Ragini MathurMost Latin American stocks dipped on Monday as fresh U.S.-Iran tensions and concerns over persistent global inflation kept investors cautious ahead of key U.S. consumer-price data later this week.Iran threatened to target energy infrastructure across the Middle East i…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P and Ragini Mathur"]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American stocks dipped on Monday as fresh U.S.-Iran tensions and concerns over persistent global inflation kept investors cautious ahead of key U.S. consumer-price data later this week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Iran threatened to target energy infrastructure across the Middle East if the U.S. launches further attacks on its assets, underscoring the risk of a broader conflict and dimming hopes for a diplomatic breakthrough."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brent crude climbed to a six-week high as supplies from the region were sharply curtailed. Elevated oil prices could add to global inflation pressures, cloud the economic outlook and push central banks toward a more restrictive policy stance."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's index of Latin American equities (.MILA00000PUS) slipped 0.2%. Markets in Brazil, the region's largest economy, were closed for the country's Independence Day holiday, contributing to thin trading volumes."]},{"type":"p","children":["The region's currency gauge (.MILA00000CUS) edged 0.1% lower, despite a 0.2% decline in the U.S. dollar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}},". Investors are now focused on U.S. inflation data due later this week, which could offer fresh clues on the Federal Reserve's interest-rate path."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"A more hawkish Fed would likely initially support the U.S. dollar,\" UBS analysts said in a note, adding that the nature of that support would depend on the backdrop behind further rate hikes."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Inflation-led tightening alongside weaker growth would present a more mixed outlook, as higher yields may start to compete with concerns about fiscal sustainability and the longer-term economic outlook.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["Following a strong U.S. jobs report last week, traders have increased bets that the Fed will raise rates at its September 15-16 meeting."]},{"type":"p","children":["U.S. President Donald Trump added to market uncertainty on Friday, saying he would halt trade with countries with which the U.S. runs a deficit unless the Fed cuts interest rates."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Brazil, political developments remained in focus. The opposition prepared for demonstrations as right-wing presidential hopeful Senator Flavio Bolsonaro sought to capitalize on a crisis engulfing the country's Supreme Court to build momentum against leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva ahead of next month's election."]},{"type":"p","children":["Recent polls showed Lula's lead over Bolsonaro narrowing. Investors generally view Bolsonaro as the more market-friendly candidate amid concerns over Brazil's deteriorating fiscal outlook."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Chile, the world's largest copper producer, copper exports totaled $4.63 billion in August, down 3.2% from a year earlier, central bank data showed. MSCI's Chile equity index (.MICL00000PUS) edged lower, while the Chilean peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," was flat."]},{"type":"p","children":["Chile's central bank is expected to leave interest rates unchanged at its policy meeting on Tuesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Mexico's benchmark stock index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}," and the peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDMXN","text":"FX_IDC:USDMXN"}}," fell 0.2% and 0.3%, respectively."]},{"type":"p","children":["Trading was subdued, with U.S. markets closed for the Labor Day holiday."]},{"type"